 out of the five cases that I  presented for them were of your  in background one was a Latina so I  think you know there is there's  certainly an issue with you know being  able to recruit sort of a more diverse  patient group and again there's  something I was sort of trying to get  out when I explained how you know these  patients are are not your average  patients they're highly educated they  have high incomes they are very savvy  you know they've worked the medical  system up until this point on their  diagnostic Odyssey and you can so I  think you know but in addition to that  and something I didn't mention but i  think is it's important and it thanks  for the question because it gives me a  chance to mention it is that you know  making sure there's a diverse sort of  ethnic racial representation in these  studies is critical  okay I'm not seeing any more questions  at this point but I'll wait a couple  more minutes if any of you have  questions please send me your questions  all right I'm not seeing any more  questions at this point of course feel  free to to email me if you if you have  any questions my email is C loss so CBL  OSS 15 at scripps edu i'm happy to to to  answer questions via email and i really  appreciate your attention and thinking  i'd like to thank the conference  organizers for inviting me to present  thank you very much
 

